        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c171b384-3065-58f4-9eaa-5c8d92988848",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon\n- People: George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon\n- Works: What Is Property?\n- Concepts: mutualism, federalism, property, anarchist philosophy\n- Places: France\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- In 1840, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon first published What Is Property?, a nonfiction work about property and its relation to anarchist philosophy.\n- After the French Revolution of 1848, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and thereafter described himself as a federalist.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- On 16 December 1911 in France, George Valois and Édouard Berth founded the political group Cercle Proudhon.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Proudhon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
